   "source": "brief",
   "text": "5. Measurement standards for agent claims. Much of the 2026 literature reports single-run deltas smaller than the noise floor measured here. A contribution could be a protocol — paired designs, null replicates, minimum detectable effect — plus a re-examination of published claims under it. This is a methods contribution and must be judged as one: it needs to overturn or qualify specific existing results to be interesting."
  },
  {
   "idea": "coadaptation_transplant_ccr",
   "sim": 0.552,
   "source": "brief",
   "text": "Memory can be one-sidedly harmful. In a controlled paired evaluation, injecting a full retrieved memory bank fixed zero items and broke six to seven (McNemar p=0.031 and p=0.016, replicated across independent runs). Noise scatters in both directions; this did not. The harm is a real phenomenon, not variance."
  },
